  embraced how stupid the plot was even  though it was actually based on true  story  but if you consider how much our  community and how how much our society  has just changed in the last 30 to 40  years  how is could it change over the next  four five hundred years  especially as in this storyline the  earth has had a massive nuclear conflict  world war iii  and obviously has then been invaded by  an alien threat  society might have changed massively  how does he then adapt to that is going  to be a really interesting plotline so  the legal battle  the basic problem comes from the fact  that this is a very old character  now the family the nolan family saying  they own the rights  their grandad wrote to the original  story therefore they own the character  of book rogers  however it's not quite that simple  one of the producers supposedly for the  new series is john f dill now john f  dill's grandad was one of the creators  of the comic strip  legendary pictures say they solely own  the rights to book rogers skydance say  they do and have issued a cease and  desist letter to legendary pictures  saying you are not to make this series  you must stop all action immediately  where it gets a little bit even more  complicated however if when you've got a  character that's 100 years old copyright  laws get a little bit  fuzzy  if you think about the sherlock holmes  character the arthur conan doyle  estate own elements to that story they  copyrighted elements to the original  stories  but they don't really own the character  sherlock holmes this is why netflix can  produce anola homes  we get other series that are based in  and around the character and they don't  have to pay the doyle family estate  massive  royalty fees  a lot of the character exists within the  public domain and that complicates  copyright law so that basically means we  could see both of these projects  actually come to fruition but let's be  honest neither of the production  companies are going to want the other  one to do it because it's going to  affect their profits so there is almost  certainly going to be a massive legal  battle and probably one of the main  reasons why this project hasn't really  moved on since back in january when it  was announced  but what is the main thing we have to  see if this series is rebooted  what is the number one thing you  remember from book rogers in the 25th  century  it's the thunder fighter  that fighter is one of the best designs  in sci-fi for me it's right up there  with like the x-wing or a tie fighter or  the viper from battlestar galactica  interesting pointing glen a larson  obviously produced both these shows  battlestar galactica and book rogers in  the 25th century they shared a lot of  the props to save money they used they  recycled a lot of the um props and the  the um sets and things  the design for the thunder fighter  though  was actually the original concept design  for the viper the viper was supposed to  look like this this design has to come  back it was one of my favorite designs  when i was a kid i had the toy  and if they don't bring it back that  will be a crime against all of scifi and  we will have to punch george clooney in  the face for it  so  what do i think is this show going to  come back  i think almost certainly yes  in what guys and what the legal battle  is between now and then i don't know but  i could see a stream of service like  netflix being desperate for this show  they  badly need content and they always  looking for that next big thing  and this so could be it  star trek its popularity is pretty good  at the moment but there's always that  threat of getting a bit bored of it we  had voyager and then we had enterprise  and people got a bit of star trek  fatigue and i think there's a risk of  that again  so we'll be looking for that next big  thing that next big sci-fi project  this could be that  and it really does give the opportunity  for a really nice balance between the  drama and certain comedy elements that  really i think make a beautiful sci-fi  show but also that reflects society and  i know people are going to say oh  they're going to make it work they'll  make book rogers a woman i don't care  really if they do or not if it's  relevant to the show  but there are elements within our  divided society the book rodgers in the  25th century could exploit and could  reflect within the show to make it a  really interesting project  so i hope they do bring back book rogers  in the 25th century  if you are new to the channel please  like subscribe hit that bell  notification so you see all of our new  videos pop up it really really helps us  out  [Music]
 

